[Event "Caro-Kann: Classical"]

{Black plays ...c6 and ...d5 to keep a solid structure, then develops the light-squared bishop before ...e6.}
1. e4 {Takes the centre.}
1... c6 {[%cal Gc6d5] Prepares ...d5 with pawn support.}
2. d4 {Takes the full centre.}
2... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] Challenges e4.}
3. Nc3 {Defends e4.}
3... dxe4 {Black gives up the centre to free the c8-bishop.}
4. Nxe4 {Recaptures.}
4... Bf5 {[%cal Gf5e4] The Classical. It develops with tempo on the e4-knight.}
5. Ng3 {[%cal Gg3f5] Gains time on the bishop.}
(5. Nc5 {Attacks b7.}
 5... e5 {Counterattacks in the centre.}
 6. Nxb7 {Takes the pawn.}
 6... Qc7 {[%cal Gc7b7] Traps the knight.}
 7. Nc5 {The knight escapes.}
 7... Bxc5 {Trades.}
 8. dxc5 {Recaptures.}
 8... Qa5+ {Regains the pawn.})
(5. Bd3 {Gambits d4.}
 5... Qxd4 {Accepts.}
 6. Nf3 {Development with tempo.}
 6... Qd8 {Retreats.}
 7. Qe2 {Development.}
 7... e6 {Solid.})
5... Bg6 {Retreats.}
6. h4 {[%cal Gh4h5] Threatens h5, which would trap the bishop.}
6... h6 {Makes room on h7.}
7. Nf3 {Development.}
7... Nd7 {Prevents Ne5.}
8. h5 {Gains space.}
8... Bh7 {Retreats.}
9. Bd3 {Offers a trade of the light-squared bishops.}
9... Bxd3 {Trades.}
10. Qxd3 {Recaptures.}
10... e6 {Solid.}
11. Bd2 {Development.}
11... Ngf6 {Development.}
12. O-O-O {Opposite-side castling.}
12... Be7 {Development.} *

[Event "Caro-Kann: Advance"]

{White gains space with e5. Black develops the bishop to f5 and attacks the d4 pawn base with ...c5.}
1. e4 {Takes the centre.}
1... c6 {Prepares ...d5.}
2. d4 {Takes the centre.}
2... d5 {Challenges e4.}
3. e5 {[%csl Gd6,Gf6] The Advance: White gains space.}
3... Bf5 {The bishop develops before ...e6.}
4. Nf3 {The Short system.}
(4. Nc3 {Prepares g4.}
 4... e6 {Solid.}
 5. g4 {[%cal Gg4f5] Hunts the bishop.}
 5... Bg6 {Retreats.}
 6. Nge2 {Prepares Nf4.}
 6... c5 {Counterattack.}
 7. h4 {[%cal Gh4h5] Threatens h5.}
 7... h5 {Stops h5.}
 8. Nf4 {[%cal Gf4g6] Hits the g6-bishop.}
 8... Bh7 {Retreats.})
(4. h4 {Hunts the bishop.}
 4... h5 {Stops h5.}
 5. c4 {Strikes at d5.}
 5... e6 {Solid.}
 6. Nc3 {Development.}
 6... Ne7 {Heads for f5.}
 7. Nge2 {Development.}
 7... dxc4 {Captures.})
4... e6 {Solid.}
5. Be2 {Development.}
5... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Attacks d4.}
6. Be3 {Supports d4.}
6... Qb6 {[%cal Gb6b2] Hits b2.}
7. Nc3 {Development.}
7... Nc6 {Pressure on d4.}
8. O-O {White castles and offers b2. Taking it with 8...Qxb2?! is risky because of Nb5 and Nc7+, so a solid move like ...cxd4 or ...Nh6 is wiser.} *

[Event "Caro-Kann: Exchange & Panov"]

{The Exchange gives a symmetrical structure, where Black's comfort comes from active pieces. In the Panov, White plays with an isolated pawn.}
1. e4 {Takes the centre.}
1... c6 {Prepares ...d5.}
2. d4 {Takes the centre.}
2... d5 {Challenges e4.}
3. exd5 {The Exchange.}
3... cxd5 {Recaptures.}
4. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3h7] Aims at h7.}
(4. c4 {The Panov.}
 4... Nf6 {Development.}
 5. Nc3 {Development.}
 5... e6 {Solid.}
 6. Nf3 {Development.}
 6... Be7 {Development.}
 7. cxd5 {Captures.}
 7... Nxd5 {Recaptures, blockading d5.})
4... Nc6 {Development.}
5. c3 {[%csl Gd4] The Carlsbad structure.}
5... Nf6 {Development.}
6. Bf4 {Development.}
6... Bg4 {Active development.}
7. Qb3 {[%cal Gb3b7] Hits b7.}
7... Qd7 {Defends.}
8. Nd2 {Development.}
8... e6 {Solid.} *

[Event "Caro-Kann: Two Knights"]

{White develops fast with Nc3 and Nf3. Black's ...Bg4 and ...Bxf3 lines give a solid structure.}
1. e4 {Takes the centre.}
1... c6 {Prepares ...d5.}
2. Nc3 {Development.}
2... d5 {Challenges e4.}
3. Nf3 {Development.}
3... Bg4 {[%cal Gg4f3] Pins.}
4. h3 {Questions the bishop.}
4... Bxf3 {Trades.}
5. Qxf3 {Recaptures. White has the bishop pair.}
5... e6 {Solid.}
6. d4 {Takes the centre.}
6... Nf6 {Development.}
7. Bd3 {Development.}
7... dxe4 {Captures.}
8. Nxe4 {Recaptures.}
8... Qxd4 {Takes a pawn.}
9. c3 {[%csl Gd4] Gambit play.}
9... Qd8 {Retreats.} *

[Event "Caro-Kann: Fantasy 3.f3"]

{The Fantasy Variation (3.f3) supports e4 with a pawn. Black's most reliable reply is 3...e6, preparing ...c5 or ...Bb4, while 3...dxe4 4.fxe4 e5 is the direct counter.}
1. e4 {White takes the centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c6 {[%csl Gd5] The Caro-Kann: prepares ...d5 without blocking the c8-bishop.}
2. d4 {Builds the ideal centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] Challenges e4. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. f3 {[%csl Ge4] The Fantasy: e4 is held by a pawn, but the f3 pawn takes the knight's best square and weakens e3 and the a7–g1 diagonal.}
3... e6 {Solid. Black prepares ...Bb4 or ...c5, and ...Qb6 can target the weak diagonal toward g1.}
 (3... dxe4 {The direct approach. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on f3.}
4. fxe4 {Recaptures with a big centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
4... e5 {[%cal Ge5d4] Hits the centre at once, exploiting White's loose kingside.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5.}
5... exd4 {Takes.}
6. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4f7] White plays for development and the f-file, offering a pawn for activity.}
)
4. Nc3 {Defends e4. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5.}
4... Bb4 {[%cal Gb4c3] Pins the knight, putting more pressure on e4.}
5. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Bxc3+ {Gives up the bishop pair to double the c-pawns.}
6. bxc3 {Recaptures toward the centre.}
6... dxe4 {Takes on e4. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on f3.}
7. fxe4 {Recaptures. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
7... e5 {[%cal Ge5d4] Strikes the overextended centre. Black has a solid game against White's loose pawns.} *
